KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp26
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ placement new in a constant expression: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
C++26 permits a placement new-expression in a constant expression when the
placement argument points to an object of a similar type whose lifetime
began in the evaluation ([expr.const]/10.18.2).  CBMC's constant evaluator
did not evaluate it: W<f()> failed to type-check (CONVERSION ERROR).
Checked with GCC 16.
